Z||000012||LZeitgeist||11-16-2001||03:17 PM||||365 is the model number for the Daytona? I never knew that.<P>I'd also heard that Ferrari never made a convertible Daytona - all the convertibles you see are either kitcars (like the ones they used on Miami Vice) or aftermarket installations... is this true?<P>I'd also heard that the white Testarossa used on MV was actually a Pantera rebody, not an actual Ferrari... I think I read that in Road & Track or something a while back... is this true also?<P><BR>(I still lust after that Scarab cigarette boat... love it, loooooove iiit...)<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000013||rogergarrison||11-16-2001||04:38 PM||||Other than both Ferraris on MV were replicas, I dont know much more. The 365 Daytona was sold as Spyder (conv) and the hardtop is actually rarer. There also was a limited number of 'factory' altered TestaRossa Spyders too. The european Daytonas had concealed headlines behind a translucent panel, the US versions had pop up type. Also all Daytonas had Ferraris racing V12 with 6 double throat carbs, no air cleaners. (just screens in velocity stacks) They sound incredible.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||11-16-2001||05:08 PM||||I have an old road and track article that says the reason they blew up the Ferrari spyder(in M.V) in favour of the testarossa is that Enzo himself got word that they were using a fake ferrari on TV and gave the show 2 cars. They were later returned to Ferrari , one of them showed up in hemmings 2 years ago with all documentation, autographed by the actors (woo hoo!)<P>Automobile magazine had an article on a company that built Testarossa converts ..you have to have brass balls to take a saw zaw to a ferrari. And from the pictures they were usinga saw zaw..Scary... I Know ASC took a swing at convert ferrari's but said the cost couldn't be justified, I believe they sold 5 cars at $85,000 over list.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000015||TRiAD||11-16-2001||05:18 PM||||Ferrari made VERY few (like 2 or 3) convertible Daytonas, and the Testarossa they used on Miami Vice (other than the "let's tear it up" shots) was real. <P>You can tell which they're using, because the kit always has cheap-o wheels, and looked like a kit. On most of the other shots, they used a real TR. ||||reg||1
